Upstream LiteLLM also ships an "enterprise/" directory under a separate
commercial license (the BerriAI Enterprise License). That directory was NOT
copied into HangarLLM, and no code from it is distributed here. The features
it provided (email alerting, PagerDuty, secret detection, moderation and
keyword guardrails, audit log endpoints, custom SSO and auth hooks, managed
files and vector stores, batch and responses cost tracking, and others) were
reimplemented independently for HangarLLM and are released under the MIT
License together with the rest of this repository.

The license-key gate that upstream applied to "premium" features in the MIT
licensed code was removed. Every feature is available to every deployment.

